From f772157bdc1755647fd339695989098be798a300 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dotheroes <dotheroes@localhost>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:01:12 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 94/96] PPU loads: the poll-word test as its own branch

vm_read32_mm tested the GCM ref-poll word inside the range test's condition
(a && b). The compiler built the poll comparison into a flag ahead of the
range branch and tested it after: cmp, sete, test and jne on every 32-bit
load, integer and float. Tested first and on its own it is one compare and
branch. The range test, the poll word's out-of-line read (which publishes
fences) and every loaded value are unchanged; a differential test of the
emitted helpers (every width, around the null page, the poll word, the
span's end, unaligned, reserved lines) prints the same output as before.

Static: a lifted chunk of 3D Dot Game Heroes at -O1 has 5.5% fewer
instructions (650,828 -> 615,042). Measured (uncapped, real audio, normal
scheduling, 5 river fights and 3 exploration runs a side, interleaved):
main-thread busy time 0.8% lower in combat frames, 2% in exploration, 1.8-2.4%
in debris frames; each within run-to-run spread (p 0.06-0.2).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 tools/ppu_lifter.py | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tools/ppu_lifter.py b/tools/ppu_lifter.py
index 40c2e63..8fbfc87 100644
--- a/tools/ppu_lifter.py
+++ b/tools/ppu_lifter.py
@@ -241,7 +241,12 @@ static inline uint16_t vm_read16_mm(const ppu_mm* m, uint64_t a)
 static inline uint32_t vm_read32_mm(const ppu_mm* m, uint64_t a)
 {
     const uint32_t ea = (uint32_t)a;
-    if (__builtin_expect(vm_mm_ok(m, ea, 4), 1) && __builtin_expect(ea != m->poll, 1)) {   /* aligned: single-copy atomic, as on Cell */
+    /* The poll word first and on its own: one compare and branch. Tested in
+     * the range test's condition (a && b), the compiler materialised it as a
+     * flag ahead of the range branch and tested it after: two more
+     * instructions on every 32-bit load, integer and float. */
+    if (__builtin_expect(ea == m->poll, 0)) return vm_read32(a);
+    if (__builtin_expect(vm_mm_ok(m, ea, 4), 1)) {   /* aligned: single-copy atomic, as on Cell */
         uint32_t v;
         if (!(ea & 3u)) v = __atomic_load_n((const uint32_t*)(m->vb + ea), __ATOMIC_RELAXED);
         else memcpy(&v, m->vb + ea, 4);
